.TH "RTCDTMFSENDER.TONECHANGE_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCDTMFSender.tonechange_event \- RTCDTMFSender: tonechange event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]tonechange\f[B]\f[R] event is sent to an
\f[CR]RTCDTMFSender\f[R] by the WebRTC API to indicate when DTMF tones
previously queued for sending (by calling
\f[CR]RTCDTMFSender.insertDTMF()\f[R]) begin and end.
.PP
To determine what tone started playing, or if a tone stopped playing,
check the value of the event\(cqs \f[CR]tone\f[R] property.
.PP
This event is not cancelable and does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqtonechange\(dq, (event) => { })

ontonechange = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
An \f[CR]RTCDTMFToneChangeEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
This example establishes a handler for the \f[CR]tonechange\f[R] event
which updates an element to display the currently playing tone in its
content, or, if all tones have played, the string \(lq<none>\(rq.
.PP
This can be done using \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
dtmfSender.addEventListener(\(dqtonechange\(dq, (ev) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]let\f[R] tone = ev.tone;
  \f[B]if\f[R] (tone === \(dq\(dq) {
    tone = \(dq&lt;none&gt;\(dq;
  }

  document.getElementById(\(dqplayingTone\(dq).innerText = tone;
});
.EE
.PP
You can also just set the \f[CR]ontonechange\f[R] event handler property
directly:
.IP
.EX
dtmfSender.ontonechange = (ev) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]let\f[R] tone = ev.tone;
  \f[B]if\f[R] (tone === \(dq\(dq) {
    tone = \(dq&lt;none&gt;\(dq;
  }

  document.getElementById(\(dqplayingTone\(dq).innerText = tone;
};
.EE
